1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,921
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:13,722
[Emilia] <i>You know what to do.</i>
<i>Finish her off.</i>

3
00:00:13,805 --> 00:00:16,182
-[gunshot rings out]
<i>-Get out of here.</i>

4
00:00:16,266 --> 00:00:18,935
<i>Don't ever come back</i>
<i>to Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

5
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:20,770
[Raul] <i>You killed them all off?</i>
<i>A whole family?</i>

6
00:00:20,854 --> 00:00:22,439
<i>You didn't even spare the kid.</i>

7
00:00:22,522 --> 00:00:25,984
<i>Do you know the way to San Marcelino?</i>
<i>How do I get there?</i>

8
00:00:26,067 --> 00:00:27,402
[tricycle driver] <i>Hop in. Come on.</i>

9
00:00:27,485 --> 00:00:28,987
<i>Mister, I'm going to get out!</i>

10
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:30,196
[blows whistle]

11
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:32,741
[Jepoy] <i>There are lots of thugs</i>
<i>around here.</i>

12
00:00:32,824 --> 00:00:36,202
<i>Anyway, I gotta go. I'm the parking boy!</i>

13
00:00:36,286 --> 00:00:37,996
<i>-Jepoy.</i>
-[car horn honking]

14
00:00:38,079 --> 00:00:42,333
[Diego] <i>To the people</i>
<i>who know where Lily is…</i>

15
00:00:42,417 --> 00:00:44,878
[Julio] <i>Idiot! You caused a huge scandal!</i>

16
00:00:44,961 --> 00:00:48,673
<i>People are talking about</i>
<i>a child who's gone missing</i>

17
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:50,383
<i>from Poblacion Ardiente!</i>

18
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:52,510
[Prianka] <i>You can't go back to Ardiente</i>

19
00:00:52,594 --> 00:00:54,179
<i>while you're still weak.</i>

20
00:00:54,262 --> 00:00:57,724
<i>I want justice for my parents!</i>

21
00:00:57,807 --> 00:00:59,684
[in English] <i>Then we have a deal.</i>

22
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:03,354
[in Taglish]<i> I've adopted you.</i>
<i>You'll be called Ivy Aguas.</i>

23
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:07,692
<i>-Something grew.</i>
-<i>A lone blossom. </i>[English] <i>A wildflower.</i>

24
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:10,695
[in Tagalog] <i>What's important</i>
<i>is it can thrive anywhere.</i>

25
00:01:10,779 --> 00:01:15,784
-<i>It can survive in any weather.</i>
-[inaudible]

26
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:19,370
[Ivy] <i>This was the only way</i>
<i>for me to be reborn.</i>

27
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:21,372
<i>To become a new me.</i>

28
00:01:23,291 --> 00:01:27,796
<i>Remember everything I taught you.</i>

29
00:01:27,879 --> 00:01:31,299
<i>Do what you must do.</i>

30
00:01:31,382 --> 00:01:33,218
<i>Make them pay.</i>

31
00:01:33,301 --> 00:01:35,011
[Ivy] <i>I made a promise to my parents.</i>

32
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:38,306
<i>Now, I promise you. I'll make them pay.</i>

33
00:01:39,015 --> 00:01:41,226
[music ends]

34
00:01:43,603 --> 00:01:45,814
PRIANKA P. AGUAS

35
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:52,821
[melancholic music playing]

36
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:36,364
[Dante] <i>There'll be fewer</i>
<i>street kids in town now!</i>

37
00:02:37,157 --> 00:02:39,284
-<i>Dad.</i>
-<i>Dante.</i>

38
00:02:39,367 --> 00:02:41,786
[both sob]

39
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:55,466
-<i>Lily, get out of here!</i>
-<i>What happened to you?</i>

40
00:02:55,550 --> 00:02:57,260
-[shushes]
-<i>Hey!</i>

41
00:02:58,052 --> 00:03:00,263
<i>Lily. Run!</i>

42
00:03:04,726 --> 00:03:06,185
[woman] <i>Can you kill her?</i>

43
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:08,730
[man] <i>The governor and mayor</i>
<i>will kill us if we let her go.</i>

44
00:03:08,813 --> 00:03:10,315
-<i>Get out!</i>
-<i>Mom. Mom.</i>

45
00:03:10,398 --> 00:03:13,985
<i>You killed my husband!</i>
<i>You killed my husband!</i>

46
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:16,362
-<i>Dad, please stop!</i>
-[grunting]

47
00:03:16,446 --> 00:03:17,363
<i>Dad!</i>

48
00:03:18,406 --> 00:03:19,824
<i>That's enough!</i>

49
00:03:22,118 --> 00:03:25,788
-Viva Ardiente!
-[crowd] Viva Ardiente!

50
00:03:25,872 --> 00:03:29,792
-[Julio] <i>Viva Ardiente!</i>
-[crowd] <i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

51
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:35,465
-Viva Ardiente!
-[crowd] Viva Ardiente!

52
00:03:35,548 --> 00:03:38,760
[crowd whooping, applauding]

53
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:45,683
[wailing]

54
00:03:50,104 --> 00:03:53,441
[yowls]

55
00:04:06,996 --> 00:04:11,000
[tense music playing]

56
00:04:43,866 --> 00:04:45,326
WELCOME TO ARDIENTE TOWN

57
00:04:46,661 --> 00:04:48,204
[in English] Hello, Poblacion Ardiente.

58
00:04:49,539 --> 00:04:50,748
[in English] I'm back.

59
00:05:14,981 --> 00:05:15,940
Who's she?

60
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:27,744
[phone ringing]

61
00:05:29,203 --> 00:05:33,291
Hello? Okay. I'm on my way home. Okay.

62
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:35,043
Back to the house. Hurry.

63
00:05:47,388 --> 00:05:51,601
[tense music playing]

64
00:06:13,956 --> 00:06:16,167
UPCOMING EVENT
ARDIENTE TRADE EXPO 2017

65
00:06:18,044 --> 00:06:23,591
ARDIENTE OPENS ITS DOORS
TO ALL ENTREPRENEURS AND INVESTORS

66
00:06:29,972 --> 00:06:31,140
SIGNAL LOST
PLEASE TRY AGAIN LATER

67
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:37,855
GOV. EMILIA AND CONG. JULIO ARDIENTE

68
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:38,898
MAYOR ARNALDO ARDIENTE-TORILLO

69
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:43,027
WELCOME
GOV. EMILIA ARDIENTE

70
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:51,828
-Well? You scoundrel!
-[Raul grunting]

71
00:06:51,911 --> 00:06:56,124
I think you revel in testing my patience!

72
00:06:56,207 --> 00:06:58,292
-Get up!
-[groans]

73
00:06:58,376 --> 00:07:01,796
I honestly can't stand imbeciles like you!

74
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:04,632
-Papa!
-Do you want to get hit, too?

75
00:07:04,715 --> 00:07:07,385
No, I just want to remind you
what the doctor said.

76
00:07:07,468 --> 00:07:09,637
[in English] That you need to calm down!

77
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:12,765
[in Taglish] You need to be healthy
for the national campaign.

78
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:15,143
[in English] Calm down? Calm down?

79
00:07:15,226 --> 00:07:17,478
[in Tagalog] Because of your husband here,

80
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:19,897
there might not even be a campaign!

81
00:07:19,981 --> 00:07:22,233
[in English] What? Why? What happened?

82
00:07:22,316 --> 00:07:23,401
You…

83
00:07:23,484 --> 00:07:28,197
You better turn over the money
by next week!

84
00:07:28,281 --> 00:07:29,240
Understood?

85
00:07:30,199 --> 00:07:31,242
Imbecile!

86
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:43,546
ARDIENTE TOWN

87
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:46,466
[Arnaldo] The documents
have to be processed soon

88
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:47,675
so I can sign them right away.

89
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:49,427
-Yes, Mayor.
-[woman] The mayor's here!

90
00:07:50,052 --> 00:07:52,180
-The mayor's here.
-Hello, Mayor!

91
00:07:52,263 --> 00:07:54,098
Good afternoon, Mayor!

92
00:07:54,182 --> 00:07:56,142
Good afternoon, everyone.

93
00:07:56,225 --> 00:07:59,729
Wow, Mayor. You're so handsome!
Can I give you a kiss?

94
00:07:59,812 --> 00:08:02,565
[woman giggles]

95
00:08:02,648 --> 00:08:03,900
-Please step away, ma'am.
-Hold on.

96
00:08:03,983 --> 00:08:05,818
No, it's okay. It's okay.

97
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:06,903
Well…

98
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:09,572
I'm sorry I can't stay long.

99
00:08:09,655 --> 00:08:12,575
-I have to be somewhere.
-Sure. Thank you, Mayor!

100
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:16,412
[woman] You smell so nice, Mayor!
He smells good!

101
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:18,873
[unintelligible dialogue]

102
00:08:22,084 --> 00:08:23,628
-Mayor.
-Give me that.

103
00:08:24,337 --> 00:08:26,589
Why do they have to kiss me so hard?

104
00:08:28,841 --> 00:08:29,675
We haven't even left yet.

105
00:08:29,759 --> 00:08:32,595
Who knows what kind of infection
they've given me. Dammit.

106
00:08:35,014 --> 00:08:37,517
Mayor, Perez's men asked me
to give you this.

107
00:08:42,855 --> 00:08:43,773
ROLEX

108
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:54,242
It's authentic.

109
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:56,911
This is pretty expensive.

110
00:08:56,994 --> 00:09:00,039
Perez must badly want me
to approve his project now.

111
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:07,088
Mayor, Mr. Fernan texted. We're needed--

112
00:09:07,171 --> 00:09:08,548
Make them wait!

113
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:15,596
This is Diego's fault.
This was all his idea.

114
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:18,057
He's starting to think like a hillbilly.

115
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:21,602
Spending time with those farmers.

116
00:09:24,730 --> 00:09:27,441
Let's go. Let's get this over with.

117
00:09:28,192 --> 00:09:29,277
Let's go, Mike.

118
00:09:38,786 --> 00:09:40,079
[crowd cheering]

119
00:09:40,162 --> 00:09:41,330
ROAD CLOSED

120
00:09:45,626 --> 00:09:48,713
[woman speaking unintelligibly]

121
00:09:48,796 --> 00:09:51,173
[crowd cheering]

122
00:09:51,257 --> 00:09:52,341
-Excuse me, sir.
-Yes, ma'am?

123
00:09:52,425 --> 00:09:56,262
Is this the way
to the Ardiente Garden Resort?

124
00:09:56,345 --> 00:09:58,306
Yes, ma'am, but the road is closed.

125
00:09:58,973 --> 00:10:01,726
-Just take the other road. Gotta go.
-Thank you.

126
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:07,023
[crowd cheering]

127
00:10:10,276 --> 00:10:11,611
BURAK-RAKAN TOURNAMENT

128
00:10:11,694 --> 00:10:13,654
[action music playing]

129
00:10:18,576 --> 00:10:21,245
[crowd cheering]

130
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:33,549
[crowd cheering]

131
00:10:37,928 --> 00:10:39,513
Get up!

132
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:58,324
["Sa'Yo" instrumental music playing]

133
00:12:12,481 --> 00:12:14,358
[crowd cheering]

134
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:36,797
[woman] One!

135
00:12:36,881 --> 00:12:39,300
-Countdown!
-[all] Two!

136
00:12:39,383 --> 00:12:40,634
[all] Three!

137
00:12:40,718 --> 00:12:44,054
[cheering, whooping]

138
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:49,310
[all chanting] Diego!

139
00:12:49,393 --> 00:12:53,481
[all chanting] Diego!

140
00:12:54,273 --> 00:12:55,983
[Pandoy] Ladies and gentlemen.

141
00:12:57,485 --> 00:13:01,197
Our champion for this year!

142
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:05,993
Not only did he display
strength and wit in battle,

143
00:13:06,076 --> 00:13:10,331
he also showed that he is one
with the people of Ardiente!

144
00:13:10,414 --> 00:13:12,791
The one and only.

145
00:13:12,875 --> 00:13:16,003
Diego Ardiente…

146
00:13:18,797 --> 00:13:21,050
Torillo!

147
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:27,097
[all chanting] Diego!

148
00:13:33,103 --> 00:13:34,313
It's Diego.

149
00:13:36,232 --> 00:13:40,110
That's him. My best friend.

150
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:50,538
[young Diego] <i>Lily.</i>
<i>Thanks for helping me out.</i>

151
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:55,292
[young Lily] <i>No worries. I got you!</i>

152
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:15,312
[shouting, in English] <i>Thank you, Lily!</i>

153
00:14:15,396 --> 00:14:16,897
[shouting, in English]
<i>You're welcome, Diego!</i>

154
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:17,982
-<i>Like that?</i>
-[both laughing]

155
00:14:18,065 --> 00:14:19,817
-Let's go!
-Let's go there!

156
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:44,967
[crowd chanting] Diego!

157
00:14:47,678 --> 00:14:49,555
Now… [clears throat]

158
00:14:49,638 --> 00:14:55,144
as per tradition, it's time
for you to give these flowers

159
00:14:55,227 --> 00:14:59,273
to the person you'd like
to dedicate your victory to.

160
00:14:59,356 --> 00:15:01,984
[crowd cheering, applauding]

161
00:15:05,237 --> 00:15:09,533
[crowd chanting] Diego!

162
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:12,703
[chanting] Diego!

163
00:15:12,786 --> 00:15:14,788
-[Loring giggles]
-[Pandoy laughs]

164
00:15:14,872 --> 00:15:16,707
-[Pandoy] Diego!
-[crowd applauding]

165
00:15:20,628 --> 00:15:22,087
[Loring] Hey!

166
00:15:26,675 --> 00:15:29,803
[in English] Miss! Miss!

167
00:15:30,804 --> 00:15:32,097
[in Taglish] Miss, wait up!

168
00:15:37,561 --> 00:15:39,563
-[in English] Miss?
-[in English] Yes?

169
00:15:41,899 --> 00:15:42,983
Uh…

170
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:47,571
[stutters] For you.

171
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:02,962
Oh!

172
00:16:03,879 --> 00:16:05,172
[in English] Sorry.

173
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:22,356
[in Tagalog] Thank you.

174
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:25,818
[Pandoy] Diego! Hey, Diego.

175
00:16:27,069 --> 00:16:28,737
Diego, your brother's here.

176
00:16:32,116 --> 00:16:33,367
Who's she?

177
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:35,369
[car engine starts]

178
00:16:35,452 --> 00:16:36,495
I don't know.

179
00:16:37,663 --> 00:16:39,790
-I didn't get her name.
-[scoffs]

180
00:16:39,873 --> 00:16:42,793
Always the slowpoke. Come on!

181
00:16:43,585 --> 00:16:45,170
Hey!

182
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:53,429
[sighs]

183
00:17:07,609 --> 00:17:09,528
[Arnaldo] I promise you.

184
00:17:10,320 --> 00:17:14,533
[in Taglish] Constructing an export
processing zone in our town

185
00:17:14,616 --> 00:17:18,495
will only help flourish
the co-op my brother started.

186
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:20,330
[crowd applauding]

187
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:23,125
Everyone's life will prosper.

188
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:25,335
[crowd applauding]

189
00:17:25,419 --> 00:17:27,963
Here's to a more progressive
Poblacion Ardiente!

190
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:29,965
[crowd cheering, applauding]

191
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:33,135
To a brighter and better future
for all of us!

192
00:17:33,218 --> 00:17:36,096
-[crowd cheers, whoops]
-Long live the mayor!

193
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:37,931
-Long live the mayor!
-[chuckles]

194
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:39,892
Thank you! Thank you so much.

195
00:17:39,975 --> 00:17:41,268
-[Arnaldo] Thank you.
-[man] Mayor!

196
00:17:41,351 --> 00:17:44,688
-[woman] Well done!
-Thank you. Thank you very much.

197
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:46,732
Thanks, Mayor!

198
00:17:46,815 --> 00:17:47,816
[chuckles]

199
00:17:48,484 --> 00:17:51,653
You're lucky you weren't struck
by lightning.

200
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:54,073
How many decades has our family

201
00:17:54,156 --> 00:17:56,492
been telling these people
that their lives will get better?

202
00:17:56,575 --> 00:18:00,370
At least I don't have to roll
in the mud to make them love me.

203
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:07,252
[sighs] Oh, well. Let's go.

204
00:18:25,729 --> 00:18:27,856
It's good we were able
to get a hold of these

205
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:30,109
so I can make a nice snack.

206
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:32,444
-You picked nice ones, too.
-Goodness, Diego!

207
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:33,821
-Nanny Loring!
-Hi, Diego!

208
00:18:33,904 --> 00:18:37,574
There you are! I thought you went home
after the wrestling match.

209
00:18:38,617 --> 00:18:43,622
Wait. Who was the girl
you gave the flowers to?

210
00:18:43,705 --> 00:18:47,334
Don't nag him.
He didn't even get her name.

211
00:18:47,417 --> 00:18:49,753
I think she was a tourist.
Someone who lost her way.

212
00:18:49,837 --> 00:18:54,800
Oh. A wildflower for a lost lady.

213
00:18:54,883 --> 00:18:57,511
-Ah.
-You're just jealous.

214
00:18:57,594 --> 00:18:59,721
-Jealous?
-Someone's jealous.

215
00:18:59,805 --> 00:19:01,807
-Is that true?
-No, I'm not!

216
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:02,808
[both chuckling]

217
00:19:02,891 --> 00:19:05,727
-But Nanny Loring.
-No, I'm not.

218
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:08,522
I just always give you
the flowers whenever I win.

219
00:19:08,605 --> 00:19:10,983
-Mm-hm.
-I wanted to turn things around.

220
00:19:11,066 --> 00:19:12,651
-[in English] For a change.
-[in English] Yeah.

221
00:19:12,734 --> 00:19:15,279
[in English] For a change. Change is good.

222
00:19:15,362 --> 00:19:17,865
[Loring, in English] For a change?
[in Tagalog] Stop messing around.

223
00:19:17,948 --> 00:19:20,367
-That hurt.
-Stop making fun of me.

224
00:19:21,243 --> 00:19:23,495
-Well, speaking of change.
-Yeah?

225
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:27,124
[in Taglish] What is this
export processing plant

226
00:19:27,207 --> 00:19:30,002
your brother told us about?
Explain it to us.

227
00:19:30,085 --> 00:19:31,628
I'm not sure, either.

228
00:19:31,712 --> 00:19:33,714
But don't worry. I'll find out.

229
00:19:33,797 --> 00:19:35,757
Ever since he became mayor,

230
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:38,093
everyone's lives seemed
to get better, didn't it?

231
00:19:38,177 --> 00:19:41,722
But let's not forget how important it is

232
00:19:41,805 --> 00:19:45,058
that Diego founded the cooperative

233
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:47,519
once he graduated college.

234
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:48,645
[in English] Of course.

235
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:52,232
And we'll only make it flourish.

236
00:19:52,316 --> 00:19:55,277
[in Taglish] And if his export
processing plant can help,

237
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:57,529
then that'll be great for all of us.

238
00:19:57,613 --> 00:20:01,408
Maybe. Maybe your brother's
changed for the better.

239
00:20:02,034 --> 00:20:05,954
I think he changed
after studying in America.

240
00:20:06,038 --> 00:20:06,997
Sometimes,

241
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:13,754
I forget all those times
he used to make my blood boil.

242
00:20:13,837 --> 00:20:14,880
[both chuckle]

243
00:20:14,963 --> 00:20:16,840
-Just admit it.
-That?

244
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:19,718
You're smitten by the mayor's charisma.

245
00:20:20,385 --> 00:20:24,181
Did he get any more handsome
since you left the mansion?

246
00:20:24,264 --> 00:20:28,518
No, no! No one's as handsome

247
00:20:28,602 --> 00:20:32,064
as my dearest Diego.

248
00:20:32,147 --> 00:20:34,274
[Pandoy stutters] What about me?

249
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:36,276
You? Wow.

250
00:20:36,360 --> 00:20:39,947
-Now, who's jealous?
-You wish. You're too old!

251
00:20:40,030 --> 00:20:41,323
-Why don't you spill it?
-What?

252
00:20:41,406 --> 00:20:42,574
-Admit it.
-Admit what?

253
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:45,619
You'd run inside with just
a towel on when I'd come around.

254
00:20:45,702 --> 00:20:47,496
You'd even squeal, too.

255
00:20:47,579 --> 00:20:50,082
Why were you always passing
by our backyard, anyway?

256
00:20:50,165 --> 00:20:51,875
[Pandoy] Well, I was a bit
of a Peeping Tom.

257
00:20:55,712 --> 00:20:57,965
ARDIENTE GARDEN RESORT

258
00:21:00,926 --> 00:21:02,010
[in English] Thank you.

259
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:07,683
["Sa'Yo" instrumental playing]

260
00:21:09,226 --> 00:21:16,066
[Pandoy] <i>Diego Ardiente-Torillo!</i>

261
00:21:25,284 --> 00:21:26,660
Please get my things from the trunk.

262
00:21:26,743 --> 00:21:27,744
Yes, ma'am.

263
00:21:50,017 --> 00:21:52,311
-<i>Miss, wait up!</i>
-[in English] <i>Yes?</i>

264
00:21:52,394 --> 00:21:54,021
[stutters] <i>For you.</i>

265
00:22:36,271 --> 00:22:38,523
[phone ringing]

266
00:22:39,941 --> 00:22:41,026
Hello?

267
00:22:42,027 --> 00:22:43,403
Yes, I've just arrived.

268
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:46,239
Don't worry, I'll be careful.

269
00:22:47,282 --> 00:22:48,283
All right, bye.

270
00:22:56,792 --> 00:23:01,755
[instrumental theme music playing]

271
00:23:06,134 --> 00:23:09,387
365 DAYS OF LOVE AND GUIDANCE

272
00:23:09,471 --> 00:23:14,267
-365 days?
-For a year filled with love.

273
00:23:20,315 --> 00:23:25,028
[instrumental theme music playing]

274
00:23:41,419 --> 00:23:45,590
["Sa'Yo" instrumental playing]

275
00:23:47,342 --> 00:23:49,678
ARDIENTE GARDEN RESORT

276
00:24:39,561 --> 00:24:43,440
[suspenseful music playing]

277
00:24:45,817 --> 00:24:46,818
Dad?

278
00:24:49,362 --> 00:24:52,115
-Dad?
-[Dante] Lily, listen.

279
00:24:52,199 --> 00:24:55,160
Dad. Dad.

280
00:24:55,243 --> 00:24:58,788
Promise me that you won't let yourself

281
00:24:58,872 --> 00:25:01,499
be abused or harassed by anyone.

282
00:25:01,583 --> 00:25:03,001
Yes, I promise, Dad.

283
00:25:03,710 --> 00:25:05,837
Dad? Dad!

284
00:25:07,964 --> 00:25:10,091
-Dad.
-[Camia] Lily?

285
00:25:10,175 --> 00:25:12,594
-Mom?
-Lily.

286
00:25:12,677 --> 00:25:14,930
Lily, I'm begging you. Leave this place!

287
00:25:15,013 --> 00:25:16,723
-Mom.
-Please!

288
00:25:16,806 --> 00:25:19,142
Mom! No.

289
00:25:20,018 --> 00:25:21,228
Mom!

290
00:25:21,311 --> 00:25:24,231
Mom! Mom? Mom?

291
00:25:24,314 --> 00:25:26,107
-[shushes]
-Mom!

292
00:25:26,191 --> 00:25:28,443
-You need to go.
-Mom, what's happening?

293
00:25:28,526 --> 00:25:30,320
-Run.
-Hey!

294
00:25:31,112 --> 00:25:33,949
Lily. Run!

295
00:25:34,032 --> 00:25:36,618
[gasps]

296
00:25:36,701 --> 00:25:40,789
[pensive music playing]

297
00:25:51,508 --> 00:25:52,759
Boss.

298
00:25:56,721 --> 00:25:58,682
Sir, we only--

299
00:25:58,765 --> 00:25:59,641
[grunts]

300
00:25:59,724 --> 00:26:01,184
Sir! Sir.

301
00:26:01,268 --> 00:26:04,020
[groans and grunts]

302
00:26:06,106 --> 00:26:09,484
What? You want some? Come here.

303
00:26:09,567 --> 00:26:11,695
What's this? One bag?

304
00:26:11,778 --> 00:26:13,071
Sorry, boss.

305
00:26:13,154 --> 00:26:14,447
[grunts]

306
00:26:15,490 --> 00:26:17,284
The next time you bring me
something like this,

307
00:26:17,367 --> 00:26:20,245
you'll have it worse. I don't want this!

308
00:26:20,328 --> 00:26:22,455
I want sacks of it! Do you understand?

309
00:26:22,539 --> 00:26:25,125
-Yes, sir!
-Take them to the car.

310
00:26:38,930 --> 00:26:42,934
[suspenseful music playing]

311
00:27:06,291 --> 00:27:07,334
Grandpa.

312
00:27:11,254 --> 00:27:12,839
Good evening.

313
00:27:12,922 --> 00:27:14,674
So you still come home here.

314
00:27:15,425 --> 00:27:17,093
I still live here.

315
00:27:18,094 --> 00:27:21,389
You're my family. I'm still an Ardiente.

316
00:27:26,144 --> 00:27:27,729
They say you won the tournament.

317
00:27:30,565 --> 00:27:31,566
[scoffs]

318
00:27:33,026 --> 00:27:35,028
Don't be surprised, Diego.

319
00:27:36,321 --> 00:27:38,406
This town is mine.

320
00:27:39,908 --> 00:27:43,787
It's only normal that I know
what happens in this place.

321
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:46,664
The fight was close.

322
00:27:46,748 --> 00:27:48,666
So, that's where your interest lies.

323
00:27:50,168 --> 00:27:52,045
Rolling in mud.

324
00:27:53,630 --> 00:27:56,216
Like I told you once before.

325
00:27:56,299 --> 00:27:59,427
[in Taglish] Some people
are only meant to be…

326
00:28:00,804 --> 00:28:02,680
worker ants.

327
00:28:04,391 --> 00:28:08,186
[in Tagalog] I guess that's all you are.

328
00:28:09,604 --> 00:28:11,439
I think it's better.

329
00:28:11,523 --> 00:28:14,442
At least one Ardiente
can stand with the people.

330
00:28:16,486 --> 00:28:17,612
Right, sir?

331
00:28:22,242 --> 00:28:25,161
I'll go rest now, Grandpa.

332
00:28:35,713 --> 00:28:37,715
Where have you been?

333
00:28:38,842 --> 00:28:41,302
Do you think I don't notice
that you're always missing?

334
00:28:41,386 --> 00:28:43,012
Is it a woman again?

335
00:28:43,096 --> 00:28:44,097
You don't have to kill anyone.

336
00:28:46,224 --> 00:28:49,144
[in Taglish] You're the only one Dad
is depending on for his campaign funds.

337
00:28:49,227 --> 00:28:52,522
My fundraisers don't get enough money,
even though they're legal.

338
00:28:52,605 --> 00:28:55,275
This is your only job,
and you can't even do it well.

339
00:28:59,279 --> 00:29:02,574
[in English] You know, sometimes
I wonder why I keep you around!

340
00:29:07,245 --> 00:29:09,205
We both know the reason.

341
00:29:11,040 --> 00:29:12,167
It's because you love me.

342
00:29:22,677 --> 00:29:24,220
[grunts]

343
00:29:27,348 --> 00:29:30,393
[grunts]

344
00:29:41,738 --> 00:29:46,117
[suspenseful music playing]

345
00:29:56,878 --> 00:29:59,881
[phone ringing]

346
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:04,010
Mayor. Yes, I'm on my way.

347
00:30:10,642 --> 00:30:14,687
-[melancholic music playing]
-[Ivy sobbing]

348
00:30:22,153 --> 00:30:25,156
[Dante] <i>I want you to learn</i>
<i>how to protect yourself</i>

349
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:28,076
<i>because your Mom and I</i>
<i>won't always be by your side.</i>

350
00:30:35,625 --> 00:30:37,794
Promise me you won't let yourself

351
00:30:37,877 --> 00:30:41,172
be abused or harassed by anyone.

352
00:30:41,256 --> 00:30:42,590
-Get out!
-Mom.

353
00:30:42,674 --> 00:30:46,553
You killed my husband!
You killed my husband!

354
00:30:49,973 --> 00:30:51,724
Dad, I'm sorry.

355
00:30:55,186 --> 00:31:00,441
I'm sorry it's been so long
since I came here…

356
00:31:02,652 --> 00:31:05,613
to finally visit your grave.

357
00:31:06,447 --> 00:31:08,449
[weeps]

358
00:31:08,533 --> 00:31:09,951
Dad.

359
00:31:14,581 --> 00:31:16,749
Dad, I promise…

360
00:31:20,753 --> 00:31:24,382
I will not leave this town…

361
00:31:28,386 --> 00:31:30,847
until I find out…

362
00:31:32,599 --> 00:31:35,310
why this happened to you…

363
00:31:37,979 --> 00:31:40,690
and to Mom.

364
00:31:45,528 --> 00:31:50,825
I swear to you and Mom.

365
00:32:04,464 --> 00:32:05,965
That's becoming your habit.

366
00:32:07,175 --> 00:32:08,593
It helps me sleep.

367
00:32:11,679 --> 00:32:12,722
Is this about Dad again?

368
00:32:13,890 --> 00:32:17,143
[in English] After all this time,
you still let him get to you.

369
00:32:17,226 --> 00:32:19,646
-Arnaldo.
-[in Taglish] What did he do this time?

370
00:32:20,396 --> 00:32:22,357
[in Taglish] You know,
your father is just frustrated.

371
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:24,359
[in English] He's frustrated?
What about you? Are you frustrated?

372
00:32:24,442 --> 00:32:28,029
[in Tagalog] Do you hate that Grandpa
made me run for mayor instead of him?

373
00:32:28,112 --> 00:32:31,532
[in Taglish] No, I'm just saying
you have to understand your father.

374
00:32:31,616 --> 00:32:34,452
Understand him?
Mom, he doesn't have the Ardiente blood!

375
00:32:34,535 --> 00:32:36,120
Grandpa himself said

376
00:32:36,204 --> 00:32:39,958
the strength of Poblacion Ardiente
comes from our blood!

377
00:32:40,041 --> 00:32:42,543
We gave him a chance, but what happened?

378
00:32:42,627 --> 00:32:46,422
[in Taglish] He ran for councilor
and lost! And mind you, he lost miserably!

379
00:32:46,506 --> 00:32:49,217
[in English] Now,
we can't let that bring us down!

380
00:32:49,300 --> 00:32:51,636
No, we can't let him bring us down!

381
00:32:51,719 --> 00:32:53,513
[in Tagalog] What about
the people of Ardiente?

382
00:32:53,596 --> 00:32:56,182
What about us and all we've worked for?

383
00:32:56,265 --> 00:32:58,726
[in English] Now, the sooner
he realizes that, the better!

384
00:32:58,810 --> 00:33:02,605
[in Taglish] The sooner everyone will be
at peace, especially you!

385
00:33:03,815 --> 00:33:05,483
[in English] I worry about you.

386
00:33:06,067 --> 00:33:07,068
Son.

387
00:33:08,069 --> 00:33:10,989
Don't worry, I can handle it.

388
00:33:12,907 --> 00:33:17,370
[phone ringing]

389
00:33:20,123 --> 00:33:21,040
Hello.

390
00:33:22,333 --> 00:33:24,002
[in Taglish] Yes, I'm at the cemetery.

391
00:33:26,170 --> 00:33:28,756
Yes, I know it's dangerous.
I'm on my way out.

392
00:33:32,427 --> 00:33:33,845
Dad, I'll be back.

393
00:33:43,604 --> 00:33:45,356
-Mayor.
-What?

394
00:33:46,566 --> 00:33:48,192
Were you asleep when I called?

395
00:33:48,276 --> 00:33:50,153
No, I just checked something out.

396
00:33:50,236 --> 00:33:54,449
[in Taglish] I just saw the floor plans
for the export processing zone.

397
00:33:56,034 --> 00:33:57,785
SITE PLAN

398
00:33:57,869 --> 00:33:59,454
It looks like it needs a lot of land.

399
00:34:00,455 --> 00:34:01,664
[in English] Yes, I know.

400
00:34:04,125 --> 00:34:06,711
Why don't we use the lot
of the cooperative?

401
00:34:08,921 --> 00:34:11,257
You're good. I like you.

402
00:34:11,841 --> 00:34:15,386
It hasn't been a year since
the headquarters in Manila sent you,

403
00:34:15,470 --> 00:34:18,890
but you're hardworking,
reliable, and trustworthy.

404
00:34:20,349 --> 00:34:21,476
Thank you, Mayor.

405
00:34:22,935 --> 00:34:26,439
But won't this cause a problem with Diego?

406
00:34:26,522 --> 00:34:28,399
He doesn't need to find out just yet.

407
00:34:30,610 --> 00:34:31,778
I'll take care of it.

408
00:34:36,449 --> 00:34:38,076
ARDIENTE GARDEN RESORT

409
00:34:41,204 --> 00:34:44,624
-Nanny Carlotta?
-I was so worried about you.

410
00:34:44,707 --> 00:34:47,960
I couldn't rest without you by my side.

411
00:34:48,836 --> 00:34:49,879
Nanny Carlotta!

412
00:34:49,962 --> 00:34:52,381
Don't tell me I have
nothing to worry about.

413
00:34:52,465 --> 00:34:56,094
You went to the cemetery last night,
even though it was dangerous!

414
00:34:56,177 --> 00:34:58,471
You made me so nervous.

415
00:34:59,388 --> 00:35:04,352
Don't make me go back to Manila.
I want to stay here with you.

416
00:35:04,435 --> 00:35:06,145
I don't want anything bad
to happen to you.

417
00:35:06,771 --> 00:35:11,859
Or that you'll lose yourself
now that you're back in this town.

418
00:35:20,535 --> 00:35:21,619
Arnaldo.

419
00:35:21,702 --> 00:35:23,287
Diego, you're here!

420
00:35:23,371 --> 00:35:25,289
I thought you slept at your nanny's.

421
00:35:25,873 --> 00:35:27,625
Well, I just picked up some things.

422
00:35:29,043 --> 00:35:31,712
By the way, it's a good thing
we saw each other.

423
00:35:32,421 --> 00:35:35,174
[in Taglish] About the export
processing plant.

424
00:35:36,008 --> 00:35:37,844
How will that help my men
at the cooperative?

425
00:35:37,927 --> 00:35:40,596
Diego, don't rush things, okay?

426
00:35:41,472 --> 00:35:44,016
I'll tell you the plan
when the time is right.

427
00:35:44,892 --> 00:35:47,478
Okay. I'll go ahead.

428
00:35:48,354 --> 00:35:52,567
Hey, wait! Maybe you'd like
to have some coffee?

429
00:35:53,234 --> 00:35:56,362
You can update me
on your progress at the co-op.

430
00:35:59,407 --> 00:36:00,783
[in Taglish] Maybe next time.

431
00:36:03,035 --> 00:36:03,953
All right.

432
00:36:09,750 --> 00:36:11,878
ARDIENTE EXPORT PROCESSING PLANT

433
00:36:14,297 --> 00:36:16,007
What about the house in Manila?

434
00:36:16,090 --> 00:36:19,927
I closed it off.
I gave everyone a vacation.

435
00:36:20,636 --> 00:36:21,679
[chuckles]

436
00:36:22,430 --> 00:36:25,099
Nanny Carlotta, it's only been a few days,

437
00:36:25,183 --> 00:36:26,184
and you're like this already.

438
00:36:26,267 --> 00:36:30,354
That's exactly it.
I'm so happy you're still alive.

439
00:36:31,022 --> 00:36:34,609
Yes, I am. Let's talk about things later.

440
00:36:34,692 --> 00:36:37,820
You should get some rest.
I have some errands to run.

441
00:36:37,904 --> 00:36:40,281
-I'll go with you!
-Nanny Carlotta.

442
00:36:42,116 --> 00:36:44,285
Please let me do this.

443
00:36:46,329 --> 00:36:47,371
Okay.

444
00:36:51,292 --> 00:36:56,923
[instrumental theme music playing]

445
00:37:38,130 --> 00:37:41,259
[Dante] <i>This is going to be our new home!</i>

446
00:37:41,342 --> 00:37:44,679
<i>We'll have the peaceful life</i>
<i>you've been dreaming of.</i>

447
00:38:10,663 --> 00:38:12,665
[tense music playing]

448
00:38:13,499 --> 00:38:16,168
Lily. Run!

449
00:38:18,212 --> 00:38:21,299
[tense music playing]

450
00:38:37,398 --> 00:38:42,486
["Sa'Yo" by Silent Sanctuary playing]

451
00:39:37,500 --> 00:39:39,794
[young Lily] <i>Go, Diego! Diego! Duck!</i>

452
00:39:39,877 --> 00:39:42,671
-[both] <i>Yay!</i>
-<i>That was amazing, Diego!</i>

453
00:41:34,366 --> 00:41:36,202
I know Lily will come back someday.

454
00:41:40,039 --> 00:41:41,040
I can feel it.

455
00:41:44,710 --> 00:41:46,086
She'll come back here.

456
00:42:39,056 --> 00:42:41,100
[birds chirping]

457
00:43:29,231 --> 00:43:32,735
[Diego] <i>I know Lily will come back</i>
<i>someday. I can feel it.</i>

458
00:43:32,818 --> 00:43:38,782
Fried bananas! Bananas!
Deliciously made fritters!

459
00:43:38,866 --> 00:43:42,119
Bananas… Oh, gosh.

460
00:43:42,661 --> 00:43:43,537
[Loring] Uh…

461
00:43:44,413 --> 00:43:46,874
Were you here
at the tournament the other day?

462
00:43:47,708 --> 00:43:49,918
Somebody handed you flowers, right?

463
00:43:50,002 --> 00:43:55,883
[in Taglish] Oh. You're beautiful
in person. I mean, up close.

464
00:43:55,966 --> 00:43:59,386
[comical music playing]

465
00:43:59,470 --> 00:44:02,014
Why are you staring like that?

466
00:44:02,097 --> 00:44:03,515
Huh?

467
00:44:03,599 --> 00:44:04,850
Um…

468
00:44:04,933 --> 00:44:07,311
I'm sorry, I just remembered something.

469
00:44:07,394 --> 00:44:11,065
Oh, you remember
when you looked in the mirror?

470
00:44:11,148 --> 00:44:13,442
That beautiful face! [laughs]

471
00:44:13,525 --> 00:44:14,652
Come on, pretty woman.

472
00:44:14,735 --> 00:44:18,030
Buy some fritters! These are yummy.

473
00:44:18,113 --> 00:44:21,325
You know, a teacher taught me
how to make these.

474
00:44:21,408 --> 00:44:25,454
She used to run a daycare.
Will you buy some? How many?

475
00:44:25,537 --> 00:44:28,499
Come on, lady. I swear, they're delicious.

476
00:44:28,582 --> 00:44:31,210
-I'm sorry, I'm on a diet.
-What?

477
00:44:31,710 --> 00:44:33,253
I have to go.

478
00:44:34,046 --> 00:44:35,089
[in English] Miss.

479
00:44:35,172 --> 00:44:38,342
-I'm sorry. I'll buy next time.
-Ma'am.

480
00:44:40,594 --> 00:44:41,845
On a diet, huh?

481
00:45:24,388 --> 00:45:27,558
Hey! Did you get her name?

482
00:45:28,809 --> 00:45:30,310
She didn't even buy my fritters.

483
00:45:30,394 --> 00:45:33,021
How could I start
chatting with her? My goodness!

484
00:45:33,105 --> 00:45:35,441
You're the queen of gossip,
so that's impossible.

485
00:45:35,524 --> 00:45:38,777
-That's not true!
-[Pandoy] You're getting old.

486
00:45:38,861 --> 00:45:39,695
You're the nosy one!

487
00:45:39,778 --> 00:45:41,530
-You're old!
-Pandoy!

488
00:45:41,613 --> 00:45:43,031
-Fernan!
-Hey, Mister Fernan!

489
00:45:43,115 --> 00:45:45,534
How was it? Any news?

490
00:45:45,617 --> 00:45:50,164
[in Taglish] I didn't get updates
on the Mayor's export processing zone.

491
00:45:50,247 --> 00:45:51,290
Seems like nobody's aware of that.

492
00:45:52,040 --> 00:45:53,709
Diego, have you talked to your brother?

493
00:45:53,792 --> 00:45:56,753
You're stressing yourself out too much.

494
00:45:56,837 --> 00:45:59,590
If there are no updates yet,
then it's okay.

495
00:45:59,673 --> 00:46:02,926
Arnaldo said there are
no concrete plans yet.

496
00:46:03,010 --> 00:46:06,847
So I think it might take a while.

497
00:46:06,930 --> 00:46:10,100
See, there's no plan yet, so just relax.

498
00:46:10,184 --> 00:46:11,727
[Loring] That's right. Here.

499
00:46:11,810 --> 00:46:14,438
-Have some fritters.
-Yes.

500
00:46:15,481 --> 00:46:17,733
-[Pandoy chuckles]
-Did you add jackfruit?

501
00:46:19,485 --> 00:46:22,613
[Ivy exhales sharply]

502
00:46:32,873 --> 00:46:33,874
[groans]

503
00:46:36,043 --> 00:46:38,962
I never thought that…

504
00:46:40,506 --> 00:46:41,507
[exhales sharply]

505
00:46:42,716 --> 00:46:44,593
I never thought that
it would be this hard.

506
00:46:47,179 --> 00:46:52,392
I thought seeing our house
would fuel my anger

507
00:46:52,476 --> 00:46:54,311
and make me tougher.

508
00:46:57,689 --> 00:46:59,942
But when I actually saw it…

509
00:47:01,235 --> 00:47:02,486
it just…

510
00:47:06,865 --> 00:47:08,909
It hurts even more.

511
00:47:20,504 --> 00:47:23,674
Then, I saw Miss Loring earlier.

512
00:47:27,636 --> 00:47:29,429
Did she recognize you?

513
00:47:30,514 --> 00:47:34,226
No. Because they only know Lily.

514
00:47:36,103 --> 00:47:38,397
To all of them…

515
00:47:40,691 --> 00:47:42,359
Lily is dead.

516
00:47:45,821 --> 00:47:49,658
[Carlotta] Now, Ivy is here,

517
00:47:50,701 --> 00:47:54,454
to seek justice for Lily's parents.

518
00:48:04,881 --> 00:48:07,676
[tense music playing]

519
00:48:20,480 --> 00:48:23,233
[Prianka] <i>You must know your enemies, Ivy.</i>

520
00:48:23,317 --> 00:48:25,527
Both in business and in life.

521
00:48:25,611 --> 00:48:29,406
Know every single detail about them.

522
00:48:30,449 --> 00:48:35,287
Every bit of information
you get will be helpful.

523
00:48:35,370 --> 00:48:38,874
Sometimes, you need to turn
your enemies into allies

524
00:48:39,458 --> 00:48:42,085
to get what you want.

525
00:48:42,628 --> 00:48:45,756
[in English] Intelligence is not enough.
You need to be wise.

526
00:48:47,966 --> 00:48:51,345
[tense music playing]

527
00:48:59,478 --> 00:49:02,439
[Ivy] <i>Emilia is the key</i>
<i>to what happened to Mom.</i>

528
00:49:02,522 --> 00:49:06,568
<i>But you? You are the key to Emilia.</i>

529
00:49:07,319 --> 00:49:09,571
<i>I'll start with you.</i>

530
00:49:10,405 --> 00:49:13,700
[tense music playing]

531
00:49:22,501 --> 00:49:24,044
[Arnaldo] <i>Do you know you're trespassing?</i>

532
00:49:24,127 --> 00:49:25,462
[in English] <i>This is private property.</i>

533
00:49:25,545 --> 00:49:28,131
[in English] <i>Mr. Mayor,</i>
<i>my name is Ivy. Ivy Aguas.</i>

534
00:49:28,215 --> 00:49:30,342
[Ivy in Tagalog] <i>I've laid the trap.</i>

535
00:49:30,425 --> 00:49:33,804
<i>All we need is for him</i>
<i>to walk right into it.</i>

536
00:49:33,887 --> 00:49:36,348
<i>If we look at the status of her assets,</i>

537
00:49:36,431 --> 00:49:38,183
<i>she can be an investor here in Ardiente.</i>

538
00:49:38,266 --> 00:49:39,726
-[in English] <i>Good work.</i>
-[Ivy] <i>Whose house is that?</i>

539
00:49:39,810 --> 00:49:44,690
[in Taglish] <i>What will it take, Mr. Mayor,</i>
<i>to make this property mine?</i>

540
00:49:44,773 --> 00:49:47,025
-[in English] <i>Dinner with the family.</i>
<i>-Isn't that too fast?</i>

541
00:49:47,109 --> 00:49:48,652
[Ivy] <i>I'll find out the truth</i>

542
00:49:48,735 --> 00:49:52,114
<i>about what you had to do</i>
<i>with my mother's death.</i>

543
00:49:52,197 --> 00:49:53,407
[in English] <i>You must be Ivy.</i>

544
00:49:53,490 --> 00:49:56,243
[theme music playing]
